% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the words of sellers for footwear, bags, cases and other leather goods, in
% the words of the tariff (Chapters 42 and 64). Each word cites the text
% that says what it means: the tariff's headings and notes, US Customs
% rulings, the Federal Trade Commission's Guides for Select Leather and
% Imitation Leather Products (16 CFR Part 24: what "leather" may mean on a
% bag, a belt or a shoe sold in the United States), the EU explanatory
% notes, and the description of the listings' fields (sources/listings/
% marketplace_fields_bags_footwear.txt) for what a field means. Bridges.
%
% The fields read: the kind (Item Type, Type, Shoes Type, Boot Type,
% Handbags Type, Types of bags, Shape); the material of the upper (Upper
% Material) and of the outer sole (Outsole Material); the material of a bag
% (Main Material); how high the shoe reaches (Upper coverage, Boot Height);
% a metal toe cap; waterproof; how the upper is fixed to the sole.
%
% Left out, because no saved text says what the word means for the tariff:
%   - "Storage Bags": US Customs puts storage bags in 3923 (plastics, for
%     packing), 4202 or 6307 (made up textile articles) by their design and
%     material; the word does not decide;
%   - "Protective Shell/Skin": a phone case that holds only the phone is no
%     container of 4202 (HQ H284146); the uses background reads "phone case"
%     for Chapter 39;
%   - "Sports shoes": the sports footwear of subheading note 1 needs spikes,
%     cleats or the like, and athletic footwear is the office's judgment;
%   - "Boot Height: ANKLE": an ankle boot may or may not cover the ankle;
%   - "Microfiber" (a polyester fabric or a polyurethane imitation leather),
%     "PU leather", "Velvet", "Lining Material", "Insole Material" (the
%     lining and the insole are no part of the upper's external surface,
%     CN EN to Chapter 64), "Shaft Material" (part of the upper only);
%   - "Upper fixing method: sticking" is read as cementing, which heading
%     6401 does not name (NY J84062).
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the kind *a kind*.
    *a field* is a field of the kind of shoe or bag.
    *a name* is a word for the footwear material *a material*.
    *a name* is a word for the bag material *a material*.
    *a value* is an upper coverage that covers the ankle.
    *a value* is an upper coverage that covers the knee.
    *a value* is a word for the upper fixing *a process*.
    *a value* is a word for straps across the instep and around the big toe.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    the constituent material of the upper of *a good* is *a material*.
    the constituent material of the outer sole of *a good* is *a material*.
    the outer surface of *a good* is of *a material*.
    *a thing* is wholly or mainly of *a material*.
    *a good* covers the ankle.
    *a good* covers the knee.
    *a good* incorporates a protective metal toe-cap.
    *a good* is designed to protect against penetration by water.
    the upper of *a good* is fixed to the sole by *a process*.
    the upper of *a good* consists of straps across the instep and around the big toe.

